  "notes": [
    "All 25 psalms built end-to-end with tools/build_psalm.py (data --strict first, then driver all steps). No --force used; no encoder refusals; no payload failed to fit.",
    "Psalm 119: 176 verses, 627 unique words, 950 occurrences, audio 1136.12 s / 3,929,703 B Opus, text pack 94,268 B, payload 6,842,922 B, cover 4096x4096 depth 2 (capacity 12,533,760 B, 54.6% used), cartridge 10,521,206 B. Depth 2 chosen by the encoder as designed; nothing else in the batch needed depth 2 (all others depth 1).",
    "Psalm 118 came closest to the 3072 depth-1 limit: payload 3,481,890 B = 98.9% of 3,520,512 B capacity; still fit at 3072 depth 1.",
    "Decode re-verification (independent second pass, tools/decode.py + SHA-256 byte-compare of extracted text/audio/palace/skybox): 25/25 PASS.",
    "Explicit model extraction byte-compare (Psalm 119): palace sha256 79ee05c9385a... == assets/cloud-palace.glb; skybox sha256 91f314f4ca2e... == assets/skybox.glb; audio sha256 864e623a28be... == psalms/119/audio.webm; text pack identical to tools/psalm119_data.json.",
    "Gloss coverage is cache-limited, not invented: en 100% everywhere; fr/ru strong (72.6%/68.0% of batch union words); de/hi/id/ko/pt/ar thin (0.6%-9.2%). Blanks stay blank with English fallback, per the rules. No word in the batch lacks all glosses (--strict passed for all 25).",
    "Psalm 119 scroll renders BLACK in headless Chromium only: its scroll-text canvas is 881 lines (ja) / 929 lines (en) = 68,878-72,622 px tall, past the usable 2D-canvas height; a probe canvas of that size accepts the dimensions but its 2D context draws nothing (getImageData returns transparent black). In headless WebKit the same Psalm 119 page renders the scroll correctly (screenshot verified). All other batch psalms are <=278 lines (<=21,844 px) and render in both engines. Root cause is in the shared viewer template (psalms/001/index.html, copied verbatim); not fixed here because 001 is out of scope for this batch.",
